REQUIRES: arm-registered-target
RUN: split-file %s %t.dir && cd %t.dir

Windows CE compressed .pdata: lld resolves the internal FUNCLEN/PROLOG
pseudo relocations (IMAGE_REL_ARM_CE_PDATA_FUNCLEN/PROLOG = 0x6/0x7) into
the flags word, compacts each 16-byte intermediate object record to the
8-byte IMAGE_CE_RUNTIME_FUNCTION_ENTRY layout (pFuncStart, flags), sorts by
pFuncStart, and reports the compact size in the exception data directory.

The two functions are linked in reverse address order (second first, first
second) so the check below proves the table is sorted.

NOTE: the hard-coded addresses below assume the standard CE layout
(.text at RVA 0x1000, .pdata at RVA 0x2000, Thumb symbol values carry
bit 0). If llvm-mc/lld layout details change, the CHECK values must be
re-derived from llvm-nm/llvm-objdump output rather than guessed.

Layout assumptions (CE PE32, image base 0x10000, /fixed):
  .text starts at RVA 0x1000.
    __C_specific_handler at 0x11000 (Thumb symbol value +1 -> 0x11001)
    Lsecond_data at 0x11004, second at 0x11011, ends at 0x11018
    Lfirst_data at 0x11018,  first at 0x11025, ends at 0x1102A
  .pdata starts at RVA 0x2000 (VA 0x12000).

RUN: llvm-mc -triple thumb-pc-wince -filetype=obj -o %t.second.o %S/Inputs/wince-pdata-second.s
RUN: llvm-mc -triple thumb-pc-wince -filetype=obj -o %t.first.o %S/Inputs/wince-pdata-first.s
RUN: lld-link /out:%t.exe /subsystem:windowsce /entry:first /base:0x10000 /fixed %t.second.o %t.first.o

The exception directory must report the compacted 8-byte-per-entry size:
2 entries * 8 = 0x10.

RUN: llvm-readobj --headers %t.exe | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HDR
HDR:      ExceptionTableRVA: 0x2000
HDR-NEXT: ExceptionTableSize: 0x10

.pdata after compaction and sort: [first 0x11025, 0x80000301]
[second 0x11011, 0x80000401].  word1 bitfields:
  PrologLen = 1 (single push), FuncLen = 3/4 instructions,
  ThirtyTwoBit = 0 (Thumb), ExceptionFlag = 1 (has handler).
The input order was second,first; the output is first,second (sorted).

RUN: llvm-objdump -s --section=.pdata %t.exe | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PDATA
PDATA:      Contents of section .pdata:
PDATA-NEXT: 12000 25110100 01030080 11110100 01040080

Each function's PDATA_EH pair must sit in the 8 bytes immediately before
the function's first instruction (kernel lookup:
(PPDATA_EH)(pFuncStart & ~(InstSize-1)) - 1):
  second at 0x11010: pair at 0x11008 = {0x11001 handler, 0x11004 data}
  first  at 0x11024: pair at 0x1101C = {0x11001 handler, 0x11018 data}

RUN: llvm-objdump -s --section=.text %t.exe | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TEXT
TEXT:      Contents of section .text:
TEXT-NEXT: 11000 70470000 01000000 01010100 04110100
TEXT-NEXT: 11010 b5302002 2103bdb0 01000000 01010100
TEXT-NEXT: 11020 18110100 b5102001 bd10
